{{Quote|It's no wonder that Pons Limbic, a Siniteen who frequented the Mos Eisley cantina, was nicknamed 'Brainiac.'|An entry in an artist's journal restored and expanded by the Graf Archive|<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>}}
'''Pons Limbic,''' nicknamed "'''Brainiac'''," was a [[Siniteen]] who specialized in calculating the coordinates for [[hyperspace]] jumps in his head. He frequented [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] and sat inside with fellow patrons [[Hem Dazon]], [[Bom Vimdin]], [[Arleil Schous]], and [[Braconnor Bakiska]] when the [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and the former [[moisture farmer]] [[Luke Skywalker]] entered the establishment in [[1 BBY]]. He was later present in the [[cantina]] again in [[0 ABY]] when the [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]] entered, searching for information on Skywalker's identity.

==Biography==
[[File:LimbicVimdin-2015StarWars5.png|thumb|right|250px|Pons Limbic frequented Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina.]]
Pons Limbic was a [[Siniteen]] who was nicknamed "Brainiac" for his ability to mentally calculate [[hyperspace]] jumps.<ref name="AEYNTK" /> He frequented<ref name="Alien Archive" /> [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] in the [[Mos Eisley]] [[spaceport]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]],<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> and in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|IV|1}}</ref> sat at a table in one of the [[cantina]]'s backrooms<ref name="CL" /> with a group of other patrons consisting of the [[Arcona]] [[Hem Dazon]], the [[Advozse]] [[Bom Vimdin]], the [[Defel]] [[Arleil Schous]], and the [[Stennes Shifter]] [[Braconnor Bakiska]].<ref name="AEYNTK" /> He was busy refreshing himself<ref name="GalacticFiles">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Star Wars Galactic Files|cardname=Pons Limbic|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/170092/cid/11689237/2018-Topps-Star-Wars-Galactic-Files-ANH-42-Pons-Limbic}}</ref> at the table when the [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and the local [[moisture farmer]] [[Luke Skywalker]] entered in search of a [[pilot]] to take them to the planet [[Alderaan]].<ref name="ANH" />

Limbic and Vimdin were both present in the cantina again after the [[Battle of Yavin]]<ref name="SW5">[[Star Wars (2015) 5|''Star Wars'' (2015) 5]]</ref> in [[0 ABY]]<ref name="ComicDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars (2015) 6|''Star Wars'' (2015) 6]] to [[0 ABY]].</ref> when the [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]] arrived in the establishment seeking information on the identity of Skywalker. Standing together in a crowd of patrons that Fett questioned, the pair remained silent. Eventually, [[Unidentified six-armed alien|another]] patron challenged the bounty hunter, but Fett bested the patron before receiving the information he sought by [[Torture|interrogating]] a [[Unidentified moisture farmer (Chalmun's Cantina)|human]] who tried to flee the bar.<ref name="SW5" /> Limbic was later mentioned in an [[Unidentified artist|artist's]] [[Unidentified artist's journal|journal]], which was restored, expanded, and displayed by the [[Graf Archive]]<ref name="Alien Archive" /> at some point no earlier than [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Year">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Limbic had [[Color|yellow]] [[eye]]s and pale skin.<ref name="ANH" /> He possessed an enormous [[brain]] that was capable of wonders.<ref name="GalacticFiles" />

==Skills and abilities==
Calculating hyperspace coordinates was one of Limbic's specialties, which made him an invaluable [[starship]] crew member. He was exceptionally intelligent and above average speed, with average strength, diplomatic skills, and fighting ability. He was not [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="GalacticFiles" />

==Equipment==
While at the cantina, Limbic wore a green [[Clothing|tunic]] and a black [[scarf]].<ref name="ANH" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:PonsLimbicMask-Chronicles.png|thumb|right|300px|Pons Limbic's mask was created by Rick Baker's team.]]
Pons Limbic first appeared in the [[original trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|Star Wars: Episode IV ''A New Hope'']],<ref name="ANH" /> which was released on [[May 25]], [[1977]].<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> The character was sketched by creature designer [[Rick Baker]] who then roughed out a sculpt<ref name="YouTube">{{YouTube|video=d1AAd1tsPds|text=Star Wars: A New Hope &ndash; Cantina Archeology Part 2: Behind The Scenes of the Mos Eisley Cantina &ndash; US|channel=@CredibleNerds|name=The Credible Nerds}}</ref> in clay<ref name="Archeology">{{YouTube|video=ElyMaaAFLKU|text=The Star Wars Cantina PT. 2 &#124; Full Panel #indianacomicconvention #tomspinadesigns #starwarshistory|channel=@FanXComicConventions|name=FanX Comic Conventions|date=2025-05-03}}</ref> that was finished by [[Rob Bottin]]. Limbic's costume was reused from a<ref name="YouTube" /> [[1940s|1942]]<ref name="BFI">{{WebCite|url=https://www2.bfi.org.uk/films-tv-people/4ce2b6b71e832|text=Spy Smasher (1942)|archivedate=20220121080142|nolive=1}}</ref> serial called [[Wikipedia:Spy Smasher (serial)|''Spy Smasher'']]<ref name="YouTube" />  and rented from [[Wikipedia:Western Costume|Western Costume]]. Limbic was filmed<ref name="Archeology" /> in supplemental footage shot in post-production<ref name="Beastmaster">{{InsiderCite|126|The Beastmaster!}}</ref> on a sound stage in Dovington's Hollywood studio between [[January 24]] and [[January 25|25]], 1977.<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Star Wars: The Definitive Story Behind the Original Film]]''</ref> [[Jibralta Merrill]] portrayed the character.<ref name="Archeology">{{YouTube|video=ElyMaaAFLKU|text=The Star Wars Cantina PT. 2 &#124; Full Panel #indianacomicconvention #tomspinadesigns #starwarshistory|channel=@FanXComicConventions|name=FanX Comic Conventions|date=2025-05-03}}</ref>

During production of ''A New Hope'', the character was referred to as "Brainee," "Cranium Head," and "Crater Head."<ref name="Cantina Roll Call">{{SWArchive|url=episode-iv/bts/article/f20030502/index.html|text=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases|int=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases}}</ref> In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the character's name was first used in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''.<ref name="AEYNTKOriginal">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the character was initially identified as "[[Pons Limbic/Legends|Brainiac]]" in the [[1996]] "[[A New Hope Limited]]" supplement for the ''[[Star Wars Customizable Card Game]]'' by [[Decipher]]<ref name="CCG">{{CCG|set=A New Hope Limited|cardname=Brainiac}}</ref> This was then revealed to be an [[in-universe]] nickname when the character's full name of Pons Limbic was established in the article "[[Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases]]" when it was updated for the [[2008]] [[StarWars.com]] site redesign.<ref name="Cantina Roll Call 2">[https://web.archive.org/web/20080106220722/http://www.starwars.com/episode-iv/bts/article/f20030502/indexp2.html Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases] (old version, as archived at [https://web.archive.org/collections/web.html Archive.org])</ref><ref name="Cantina Roll Call" /> The [[Wikipedia:Limbic system|limbic system]] and [[Wikipedia:Pons|pons]] are both parts of the real-life human brain.<ref name="Neurology">{{WebCite|url=https://www.brightfocus.org/alzheimers/infographic/brain-anatomy-and-limbic-system|text=Brain Anatomy and Limbic System|date=2015-06-04|work=[[Wikipedia:BrightFocus Foundation|BrightFocus Foundation]]|archivedate=20221208183927}}</ref>

[[File:Vision-Cantina.png|thumb|left|300px|Pons Limbic appeared in the cantina in the animated short film "Tatooine Rhapsody."]]
Limbic appears in "[[Tatooine Rhapsody]]," a non-canon short film in the ''[[Star Wars: Visions]]'' series<ref name="Visions">{{Visions|Tatooine Rhapsody}}</ref> released on [[September 22]], [[2021]].<ref name="Air date">{{SWYouTube|b9Gr9gKFxpE|STAR WARS: VISIONS &#124; SPECIAL LOOK &#124; DISNEY+|sw_url=video/special-look-star-wars-visions}}</ref> In the film, Limbic is shown in the Mos Eisley cantina talking to<ref name="Visions" /> [[Nabrun Leids]]<ref name="AEYNTK" /> while other patrons watch a performance by the band [[Star Waver]] on handheld [[viewscreen]]s. In addition to his green tunic<ref name="Visions" /> from ''A New Hope'',<ref name="ANH" /> Limbic is shown wearing gray pants and brown [[boot]]s,<ref name="Visions" /> which matches a Legends action figure of Limbic made by [[Hasbro]] for their [[Star Wars: The Legacy Collection|Legacy Collection]] line in 2008.<ref name="Hasbro">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: The Legacy Collection|pack=#35: Pons Limbic|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/TLC35pons.asp}}</ref>

